! Read a NON-ORTHOGONAL CIF and write it back out.
!
! Quartz is trigonal P 31 2 1, gamma = 120 degrees. Every other CIF-writing
! test in the suite has an orthogonal cell, where the crystal-to-cartesian
! ADP congruence is diagonal and mixes nothing -- which is why three separate
! ESD defects lived here unseen. This job exists to make that class visible:
!
!  . the ADP ESDs must come back unchanged, because they are written into the
!    same (crystal) frame they were read in, and ESDs are never transformed;
!  . the cartesian CIF must carry NO ESDs at all, with the note saying why,
!    because without a covariance matrix they cannot be propagated.
!
! Si1 and O1 carry esds on all six ADP components, off-diagonals included, so
! the components that actually mix under a 120 degree cell are covered.

{

   name= quartz

   output_style_options= { real_precision= 7 }

   CIF= { file_name= quartz.cif }

   process_CIF

   put

   put_cif

}
